    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0229" n="97" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg97"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 61 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President to the Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d61-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-06-14">14 [<hi rendition="#italic">15</hi>] June
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>293. Replying to your 141505,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d61-f2"/> Eisenhower has been
                    directed to make advance arrangements for accommodations and conference space
                    for American members of the forthcoming conference.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d61-f3"
                    /> He has not yet been informed of the names or number of Americans who will be
                    in my party. I intend to take with me my Chiefs of Staff, the Secretary of State
                    with his assistants, two or three other officials of high rank, servants, secret
                    service men, etc.</p>
                <p>As soon as the number and names are known, I will send them for your
                    information.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d61-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d61-f1-content">
                <p>Presumably sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy
                    channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d61-f2" n="2" xml:id="d61-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="#d60">document No. 60</ref>.</p>
            </note>
